From deec7a6fb4c25f96549fe685f880f47ef33255d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hank Yeomans <hank@quorra.taile7bcb.ts.net>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 22:32:12 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 61/61] dsv4 topk_v2: fix the cluster-path refinement (recipe
 T3.51)

The cluster path (SM90/SM100 upstream; compiled out on SM120) of the exact
top-k patch failed when exercised by forcing SUPPORT_CLUSTER on SM120:

* cluster_refine folded every warp's key AND / OR straight into one word of
  rank 0's shared memory with 64-bit atomicAnd / atomicOr over DSMEM. Updates
  were lost (the AND came back with bits no candidate shared), so a round could
  not narrow and the collect emptied: a tied row then came back as 0..511 or
  with the lowest-index survivors missing. Each rank now folds its block
  locally and writes one slot in rank 0's smem; rank 0 reduces the slots.
* The peers read rank 0's final count_gt / count_eq after bar-3 to decide
  whether to refine, while rank 0 could already have exited (small-batch
  INDICES mode) or started its next item (persistent kernel) -- DSMEM of an
  exited CTA; the persistent ragged test died with an unspecified launch
  failure. forward() now zeroes the counts after bar-0 (not before), and both
  cluster kernels end on a cluster barrier.

Upstream suite with the cluster path forced on SM120: 302 passed (was 156
failed); default path 302 passed. Regression test test_topk_v2_exact_under_ties
added (fails 14/15 on stock).

Amp-Thread-ID: https://ampcode.com/threads/T-01a0c10b-a5f8-77fc-b238-7147d12ccf29
Co-authored-by: Amp <amp@ampcode.com>
